<h1>Limitations</h1>

<p>These boundaries are first-class results, not a footer. They say where the certificate stops.</p>

<ul>
  <li>The tightest (≤ 3%) certificate is Paraformer-only. Belle’s Aishell-1 floor is α = 5%. zipformer certifies nowhere: it exposed no usable posteriors.</li>
  <li>0/20 reseeds are correlated (fixed test set, resampled calibration/tune carve). They are not 20 independent trials.</li>
  <li>Macro-CER is certified; micro-CER is reported and is not the certificate.</li>
  <li>The English arm is non-vacuous at α = 5% on the frozen carve and vacuous at tighter targets until the calibration budget grows. It is not a Mandarin landscape cell.</li>
  <li>Spontaneous and multi-domain Mandarin at WenetSpeech scale is untested.</li>
  <li>MagicData is evaluation data under CC BY-NC-ND. The archive stores derived per-utterance CER metrics, not audio or transcripts.</li>
  <li>Landscape THCHS cells (Paraformer 4.07%, Belle 6.99%, zipformer 82.15% full-set macro-CER) were measured on a mislabeled THCHS-30 mirror split (n=1339; 82.7% train-speaker audio), not the official THCHS-30 test (n=2495). A frozen data audit reproduced 3.75% / 6.62% / 81.80% on that n=1339 pool. The ~0.3 pp gap is unresolved; neither triple is a reproduced official-test number. Whisper THCHS-30 (9.93%) uses the corrected official test.</li>
</ul>

<aside class="callout">
  <p>Whisper Mandarin is honestly vacuous at every tight target (Aishell-1 full-set macro-CER 28.1%; official THCHS-30 test 9.93%). Vacuous-at-target is a published outcome, not an error state and not a silent empty accept set.</p>
</aside>
